# Playwright E2E Structure

Write independent, auto-waiting E2E tests. Specs orchestrate flows and assert outcomes; locators stay in page objects.

## Rules

- Group related cases with `test.describe` and put shared navigation/setup in `test.beforeEach`.
- One clear behavior per test. Name tests by expected outcome (`should show an error for invalid credentials`).
- Cover the success path and at least one failure/error path for critical flows.
- Tests must not depend on execution order or leftover UI/server state.
- Use Playwright auto-waiting and web-first assertions (`toBeVisible`, `toHaveURL`). Never `waitForTimeout` in committed tests.
- Isolate third-party or unstable APIs with `page.route` when the test is about UI behavior, not the real backend.
- Keep a spec focused (about 3–5 tests per feature file). Do not assert CSS/visual styles.

## Example

```typescript
import { test, expect } from '../fixtures';

test.describe('Login', () => {
  test.beforeEach(async ({ loginPage, page }) => {
    await page.route('**/api/login', async (route) => {
      const body = route.request().postDataJSON() as { email?: string };
      if (body.email === 'user@example.com') {
        await route.fulfill({ status: 200, body: JSON.stringify({ ok: true }) });
        return;
      }
      await route.fulfill({ status: 401, body: JSON.stringify({ error: 'Invalid credentials' }) });
    });
    await loginPage.goto();
  });

  test('should sign in with valid credentials', async ({ loginPage, dashboardPage }) => {
    await loginPage.login(process.env.TEST_USER_EMAIL!, process.env.TEST_USER_PASSWORD!);
    await expect(dashboardPage.heading).toBeVisible();
  });

  test('should show an error for invalid credentials', async ({ loginPage }) => {
    await loginPage.login('wrong@example.com', 'bad-password');
    await expect(loginPage.errorMessage).toBeVisible();
  });
});
```
